#!/bin/sh
HOST=$(hostname -s 2>/dev/null || echo freesounder)
cat << MOTD

freesounder player (${HOST})
------------------
This board is a locked-down appliance. There is no login password and the
first-user wizard is disabled. Use the FreeSounder app to set it up over
Bluetooth or the local network. The hostname is ${HOST}; the room name in
the app is the user-facing label.

  sudo freesounder-setup status
  sudo freesounder-setup doctor

SSH is off unless you enable developer mode from the app
(Settings → player → tap the version seven times). It turns itself off
again after a reboot.

MOTD
